+  /generation-evidence/codex-output.log | tail -n 300

codex
The static gate found two material failures with machine-checked witnesses. First, the proof-local loop rewrite is broader than its bridge-free theorem: it omits `<env>` and other constrained cells. With `<env> 0`, fixed semantics updates scope 0, but the added rule proves a false scope-1 update; the same postcondition fails without the rule. Second, supplied `lower` is ASCII-only while the claim quantifies over every `IntSeq`; U+0130 makes the modeled result 0 while the submitted CPython program returns 1. I’m completing the required independent false-postcondition mutation and trust accounting before issuing the report.
Claim pinning and witnesses passed, but exhaustive static review found a globally false over-broad operational bridge and an unrestricted-domain Unicode mismatch, each with preserved false-conclusion evidence.
  ✓ Read mandated Kit skills and validate audit infrastructure/provenance
  ✓ Check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Rebuild semantics/proof cleanly and run all positive claims
  ✓ Audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and satisfying witnesses
  ✓ Inventory and statically review every local K declaration/rule
  → Create and run a fresh meaningful non-vacuity mutation
  • Account for proven vs assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md verdict
